# Button hover glare (universal)

All interactive CTAs / pills that use a hover “擦亮” wipe must follow this stack.
This is a site-wide convention — do not invent a different hover highlight.

## Required stack (bottom → top)

1. **Button fill** — solid or translucent background on the outer shell (`GlareHover` / equivalent)
2. **Glare wipe** — the moving highlight layer (`::before` or equivalent), clipped to the pill with `overflow: hidden` + matching `border-radius`
3. **Label / icon** — text stays above the wipe (`z-index` above the glare)

Never put an opaque (or mostly opaque) fill on the child that sits above the glare — that buries the wipe (especially on dark buttons like View services).

## Pattern

```tsx
<GlareHover background="{fill}" borderRadius="999px" glareColor="#ffffff" …>
  {/* child background must be transparent */}
  <Link or SpecularButton tintOpacity={0} />
</GlareHover>
```

## Checklist

- Hover wipe is visible on dark and light fills
- Wipe is masked to capsule/pill — not a raw rectangle
- Specular / rim idle effects (if any) pause on hover so only the glare wipe shows
- Nav Contact, hero CTAs, and future buttons share this same hover language
- Wipe duration uses shared `GLARE_WIPE_MS` from `GlareHover.tsx` (do not invent a faster local duration)
